{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "JoinTwoLevels",
    "description": "A derivative through two joined sums (spec \u00a73.5): six points (recs) binned into four cells through an overlap join of the points' (X, Y) and the cells' envelopes (B, as join_regrid), then the four cells binned into two coarse cells through a second overlap join of the cells' centres (XC, YC) and the coarse envelopes (G). The coarse field reads B squared and an array parameter H; a state z integrates it. The bands of z's right-hand side with respect to q and to F pass through both joins and carry both joins' clauses."
  },
